runs.developer_explanation:
Your for‑loop will run forever because the loop variable 'i' grows while the condition only checks for non‑negative values. This results in an infinite loop. Change the loop to decrement 'i' (i--) or adjust the condition to stop when 'i' becomes less than zero. For example: 

for (int i = 5; i >= 0; i--) {
    System.out.println(i);
}
